WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.838
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:02.888 --> 00:00:06.324
AI for Young Builders, video 14.

3
00:00:06.374 --> 00:00:10.790
Final project: build and present your AI.

4
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.391
This is your moment.

5
00:00:13.441 --> 00:00:17.864
Use everything you have learned to build an AI that solves a

6
00:00:17.914 --> 00:00:19.280
problem you choose.

7
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:26.705
Every AI project goes round the same loop.

8
00:00:26.755 --> 00:00:27.431
Plan.

9
00:00:27.481 --> 00:00:29.321
Collect data.

10
00:00:29.371 --> 00:00:30.193
Train.

11
00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:30.920
Test.

12
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.083
Improve.

13
00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:32.955
Share.

14
00:00:33.005 --> 00:00:37.170
And then, often, round again.

15
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.785
Need an idea?

16
00:00:39.835 --> 00:00:44.530
A recycling sorter for paper, plastic and metal.

17
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.485
Hand signals for a no-touch quiz buzzer.

18
00:00:48.535 --> 00:00:50.066
Weather doodles.

19
00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.625
Or a reader for handwritten numbers.

20
00:00:53.675 --> 00:00:55.800
Or your very own idea.

21
00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.698
Your model’s results are attached automatically.

22
00:01:00.748 --> 00:01:05.345
Then write about the problem and who it helps, your data, your

23
00:01:05.395 --> 00:01:11.192
test accuracy and biggest mix-up, one improvement with its accuracy before and

24
00:01:11.242 --> 00:01:14.040
after, and who your AI might fail for.

25
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.348
Here is a secret: your accuracy itself is not graded.

26
00:01:19.398 --> 00:01:25.686
An honest seventy percent with good reasoning beats an unexplained hundred percent.

27
00:01:25.736 --> 00:01:31.490
Your teacher reviews your project, and you can improve it and send it again.

28
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.210
Let us recap.

29
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.088
Choose a problem and two to four groups.

30
00:01:38.138 --> 00:01:40.996
Collect, train, test, improve.

31
00:01:41.046 --> 00:01:45.843
Report accuracy honestly and think about fairness.

32
00:01:45.893 --> 00:01:51.660
Next: The final assessment, your badge and your certificate.
